# Every variable BookWorm needs, with no real values.
#
# --- Front end (Vite) -------------------------------------------------------
# Copy these to front_end/bookworm-app/.env.development.local (and set them in Vercel for production).
# Values come from the Supabase dashboard → Connect. Both are public: every VITE_ value is compiled
# into the JavaScript every visitor downloads, so never put a secret or service_role key here.
# Leave them empty to run on the built-in sample catalog with no backend.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Edge Function secrets (NOT for any .env file in the front end) ---------
# Set in Supabase only: Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets, or `supabase secrets set NAME=value`.
# Your own key from Google Cloud Console (Books API). Never in a VITE_ variable, the repo or a prompt.
GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the functions from a browser (CORS).
# Example shape: your Vercel domain plus http://localhost:5173
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are provided to functions by Supabase.
